From 0128fb3ec758a808599bcf6ed5c128003bf68bd7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hermes <hermes@local>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 11:53:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] DSML tool args stream: a string parameter's argument deltas
 now flow as the model writes them (was: the whole value held to its closing
 tag - a 10k-token write was byte-silent for minutes and pi-ai's 300000ms
 stream idle timeout killed every long tool call). DsmlRewriter streams the
 escaped JSON body with only a possible closer-prefix held back; the scanner
 gets a verbatim 'stre' state via a new <arg_stre> open; parse_tool_call
 decodes it the same. Closing-tag rule matches the reference decoder exactly
 (only the complete token is structural). Also fixes the queue-heartbeats
 counter leak: a client leaving while queued now gives back status[queued] and
 its FIFO place (test_server.GoneClients was failing since 7b093f53).
 Parser/DSML suites green incl. 3 new streaming tests; GoneClients 3x stable.

